      "body_html": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Could you please review the two #[verifier::external] annotations on the existing Send/<code class=\"notranslate\">Sync</code> impls? Verus rejects these unsafe impls within the verified code, and this PR does not prove their thread safety. Is retaining them as a trusted boundary acceptable, or should their safety be established in this PR? Is there a preferred way to handle such cases?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Verus cannot prove these annotations by itself so they must be kept <code class=\"notranslate\">verifier::external</code>, but this is acceptable as long as we can prove that the implementation is thread-safe by, e.g., the sync primitives.</p>",
      "body_text": "Could you please review the two #[verifier::external] annotations on the existing Send/Sync impls? Verus rejects these unsafe impls within the verified code, and this PR does not prove their thread safety. Is retaining them as a trusted boundary acceptable, or should their safety be established in this PR? Is there a preferred way to handle such cases?\n\nVerus cannot prove these annotations by itself so they must be kept verifier::external, but this is acceptable as long as we can prove that the implementation is thread-safe by, e.g., the sync primitives.",
